// Oscillating -- the RA-vs-WRA separating behaviour.
//
// rmm-zoo edge: RA strictly weaker than WRA (i.e. WRA is the weaker model).
// Source: Lahav & Boker, "What's Decidable about Causally Consistent Shared
//         Memory?" (TOPLAS 2022), Ex. 3.7 (Oscillating); Lahav, Giannarakis &
//         Vafeiadis, POPL 2016.
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/strictly-weaker/RA-vs-WRA/Oscillating.
//
// One reader sees x go 1, then 2, then 1 again, while two writers each write
// once. Under RA and SRA the reader's three reads are hb-ordered and mo totally
// orders the two writes, so returning to 1 after seeing 2 violates
// read-coherence. WRA has no mo, and the two writes are hb|loc-unrelated, so
// nothing forbids the oscillation.
//
// Reference verdicts: WRA ALLOWS. RA, SRA, C11, RC11 and SC FORBID
//                     (this is a coherence violation for any model with mo).
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids,
//     RA forbids, SRA forbids, WRA allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     CC allows. Equivalent to WRA on the release-acquire fragment (zoo edge
//       WRA = CC).
//     PC forbids. Coherence forbids it, and PC is stronger.
//   the models' definitions:
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD, PRAM, Causal,
//     Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, WFR. C11 and C++17 are not implemented in
//     MoRDor.
x := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel)
} ||| {
  r0 := x.load(acq);
  r1 := x.load(acq);
  r2 := x.load(acq)
} ||| {
  x.store(2, rel)
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [WRA, CC, MW]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO,
                                     Coherence, RC11, RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, RA,
                                     SRA, PC]
